snp1.5:6.1 starts: Whoever lives by the path,
snp1.5:6.2 starts: restrained, mindful,
snp1.5:6.3 starts: partaking of blameless ways,
snp1.5:6.4 starts: is called the third of monks:
snp1.6:2.1 starts: About the man in decline
snp1.6:2.2 starts: we ask Gotama,
snp1.6:2.3 starts: having come to question the Blessed One:
snp1.6:2.4 starts: What is the way leading to decline?
snp1.6:11.1 starts: The Buddha:
snp1.6:11.2 starts: a brahman, contemplative,
snp1.6:11.3 starts: or other mendicant:
snp1.6:11.4 starts: That is the way leading to decline.
snp1.6:23.1 starts: The Buddha:
snp1.6:23.2 starts: a woman given to drink & squandering
snp1.6:23.3 starts: or a man of that sort:
snp1.6:23.4 starts: That is the way leading to decline.
snp1.7:7.1 starts: Whoever, from village or wilderness,
snp1.7:7.2 starts: takes in a manner of theft
snp1.7:7.3 starts: what others claim as ‘mine’:
snp1.7:7.4 starts: He should be known as ‘outcaste.’
snp1.7:18.1 starts: Whoever, when a brahman or contemplative
snp1.7:18.2 starts: appears at mealtime,
snp1.7:18.3 starts: reviles him with speech and doesn’t give:
snp1.7:18.4 starts: He should be known as ‘outcaste.’
snp1.7:19.1 starts: Whoever, wrapped in delusion,
snp1.7:19.2 starts: speaks here what is untrue,
snp1.7:19.3 starts: greedy for whatever-the-thing:
snp1.7:19.4 starts: He should be known as ‘outcaste.’
